---
// SecurityTrust.astro
---

<section id="security" class="section-padding security-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="badge badge-emerald">Privacy & Trust by Design</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        Your data belongs to you. <span class="gradient-text">It never leaves your browser.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        Unlike cloud-synced extensions that sell browsing habits or read private form fields, StickySite is built around a zero-knowledge, local-first architecture.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="security-grid">
      <!-- Pillar 1 -->
      <div class="glass-card sec-card">
        <div class="sec-header">
          <div class="sec-icon-circle green-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="sec-title">100% Local-First Storage</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          All your saved views, filter parameters, and page configurations reside exclusively inside your device's <code>chrome.storage.local</code>. No user account is needed, and no telemetry syncs your views to cloud servers.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 2 -->
      <div class="glass-card sec-card">
        <div class="sec-header">
          <div class="sec-icon-circle purple-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
              <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="sec-title">Proactive Safety Filtering</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          StickySite scans DOM attributes and automatically blocks sensitive fields before saving. Passwords, credit cards, bank details, authentication tokens, and personal IDs are strictly ignored and never recorded.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 3 -->
      <div class="glass-card sec-card">
        <div class="sec-header">
          <div class="sec-icon-circle blue-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
              <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
              <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="sec-title">Zero Destructive Actions</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          StickySite only populates form controls and filters. It is architecturally incapable of triggering "Submit", "Pay", "Purchase", "Delete", or confirmation buttons, preventing unintended side effects.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 4 -->
      <div class="glass-card sec-card">
        <div class="sec-header">
          <div class="sec-icon-circle amber-circle">
            <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M21 2l-2 2m-7.61 7.61a5.5 5.5 0 1 1-7.778 7.778 5.5 5.5 0 0 1 7.777-7.777zm0 0L15.5 7.5m0 0l3 3L22 7l-3-3m-3.5 3.5L19 4"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="sec-title">Least-Privilege Permissions</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="sec-desc">
          No blanket <code>&lt;all_urls&gt;</code> permission upon installation. Origin access is requested on-demand only when you explicitly choose to save or restore a view on that specific website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .security-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .sec-card {
    padding: 2.25rem;
    background: #ffffff;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .sec-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 12px 28px -8px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.1);
  }

  .sec-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.15rem;
  }

  .sec-icon-circle {
    width: 46px;
    height: 46px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    border-radius: 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .green-circle {
    background: #d1fae5;
    color: #059669;
    border: 1px solid #a7f3d0;
  }

  .purple-circle {
    background: #f3e8ff;
    color: #7c3aed;
    border: 1px solid #e9d5ff;
  }

  .blue-circle {
    background: #dbeafe;
    color: #2563eb;
    border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
  }

  .amber-circle {
    background: #fef3c7;
    color: #d97706;
    border: 1px solid #fde68a;
  }

  .sec-title {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sec-desc {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .sec-desc code {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    background: #f1f5f9;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    color: #334155;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .security-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
